# Allocation baselines for the CI gate (deploy/ci/alloc-gate.sh).
#
# Allocation COUNTS and BYTES are deterministic per workload, so they gate
# hard in CI; wall time is machine-noisy and is reported but never gated.
# Ceilings are the measured steady state (docs/agents/2026-08-03-allocation-
# report.md) + ~15% headroom for legitimate drift. If a PR intentionally
# changes an allocation profile, update the ceiling IN THAT PR with a line
# in the description justifying it.
#
# Measured 2026-08-03 (post service-squash round):
#   engine mix:  16.5 allocs/tx, 3,672 B/tx
#   sequencer:    3.0 allocs/tx,   504 B/tx
#   ingress:      7.3 allocs/op, 4,254 B/op
ENGINE_MAX_ALLOCS=19.0
ENGINE_MAX_BYTES=4300
SEQUENCER_MAX_ALLOCS=3.5
SEQUENCER_MAX_BYTES=600
INGRESS_MAX_ALLOCS=8.5
INGRESS_MAX_BYTES=4900
